#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054499 :question/id #uuid "2efe9f75-18c0-5a86-b56b-3f338b7e5c2d" :question/math-academy-id "e-1702" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the graph of the straight line below?\n\nI. $y=2x-1$\n\nII. $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$\n\nIII. $2x-y=1$\n\n![](images/93/93dc9d447c15e4597549996b1f0b533cf86783b5cc5df032a4c46d4ca8934abc.png)" :question/worked-solution "Let's pick two distinct points on the line. For example, we can choose $A$ and $B$ with coordinates $(0,-1)$ and $(2,3)$, respectively.\n\n![](images/a9/a9f18453dedb1763908825301f80ef86307d3a3aceaf678bbe8579a42a0996f5.png)\n\nNow, we substitute the coordinates of both points in our equations. If both points satisfy an equation, then we can conclude that the equation represents the line in the graph. Otherwise, if any point does *not* satisfy the equation, then we can conclude that the equation does *not* represent the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation I: $y=2x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) & =2(0)-1 \\\\ -1 & =-1\\,✓ \\\\ (3) & =2(2)-1 \\\\ 3 & =3\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=2x-1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation II: $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1) & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)-1 \\\\ -1 & =-1\\,✓ \\\\ (3) & =\\frac{1}{2}(2)-1 \\\\ 3 & =0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=\\dfrac{1}{2}x-1$ is *not* an equation of the line in the graph.\n\n- Equation III: $2x-y=1.$\nSubstituting the coordinates of $A(0,-1)$ and $B(2,3),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(0)-(-1) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓ \\\\ 2(2)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $2x-y=1$ is an equation of the line in the graph.\n\nOf the given equations, the only equations that represented the line in the graph were $y=2x-1$ and $2x-y=1,$ corresponding to answer choices I and III. Therefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054571 :question/id #uuid "92c02155-ad64-59a7-be4c-052e5bdfb429" :question/math-academy-id "e-6096" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f87e0eb91b6ec47ca8a4d64c2824396e613123ed37862975b606608ff70445f0.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y=5-2x.$" :question/worked-solution "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,5), B(2,1)$ and $C(3,0).$ \n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5-2x \\\\ (5) & =5-2(0) \\\\ 5 & =5\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line:\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5-2x \\\\ (1) & =5-2(2) \\\\ 1 & =1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line:\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5-2x \\\\ (0) & =5-2(3) \\\\ 0 & =-1\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only points $A$ and $B$ lie on the line."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054602 :question/id #uuid "6b16ff95-8b78-587d-a7c8-8d0909b69f19" :question/math-academy-id "e-983" :question/problem "Use the table below to plot the graph of $y=3x-2.$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td>$0$</td>\n<td>$1$</td>\n<td>$2$</td>\n<td>$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n" :question/worked-solution "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=3x-2.$\nTherefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=3(0)-2=-2,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=3(1)-2=1,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=3(2)-2=4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=3(3)-2=7.$\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$x$</td>\n<td>$0$</td>\n<td>$1$</td>\n<td>$2$</td>\n<td>$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">$y$</td>\n<td>$-2$</td>\n<td>$1$</td>\n<td>$4$</td>\n<td>$7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/09/09e670353b2114b229769e2bd6b3eb4a9895389b818fc3f4ace6997a3e7efa3f.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=3x-2.$\n\n![](images/d2/d2d8891102ce99020f544bd8d82a5ff0454080474ce4267ef5285db92f5b2ca0.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054603 :question/id #uuid "4aad1578-4134-5f25-88cb-8ab4631257ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-984" :question/problem "Sketch the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find two distinct points that lie on our line. Any two points will do!\n\nIt is often easiest to pick one of the points to have an $x$-coordinate of $x=0.$ So, for the first point, we will let the $x$-coordinate be $x=0.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(0)+3 \\\\  & =0+3 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first point is $(0,3).$\n\nFor the second point, let's choose $x=4.$ Then the $y$-coordinate is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{2}x+3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(4)+3 \\\\  & =-2+3 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the second point is $(4,1).$\n\nFinally, we plot those two points on the $xy$-plane and draw a line through them. This is the graph of $y=-\\dfrac{1}{2}x+3.$\n\n![](images/36/36689081acaacb24a09826c3927388697e77d92caeca900d053d33d0f99d2b8c.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fed705f-0c5e-5dca-accb-bae607a4fc2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439597} {:answer/id #uuid "cb421742-e5de-572c-971a-9eb2c061f005" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439598}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fed705f-0c5e-5dca-accb-bae607a4fc2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439597} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbd232fa-3537-5420-94e8-e9051a01e549" :answer-field/key "Point $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440156} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3573bc9-ee80-5f0a-9aae-2aaa34b57dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439599} {:answer/id #uuid "6e511485-221a-58b3-bdab-2e385d1b8a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e511485-221a-58b3-bdab-2e385d1b8a79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439600} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2f3d462-8064-56af-8c8f-38267e2f50f9" :answer-field/key "Point $B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440157} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6c0980-d69d-5ad0-a62a-b3c07b27657d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439601} {:answer/id #uuid "20e7210d-dcfb-5af3-b90e-81838dff307b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6c0980-d69d-5ad0-a62a-b3c07b27657d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439601} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea9cb7b2-31c2-5b00-8722-10352ebddb97" :answer-field/key "Point $C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440158}] :question/id #uuid "591488e6-be15-5117-89a8-9b785af2738a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22405" :question/problem "![](images/c6/c63af2b4cd9209077baee74e5f4f4059bc1c8c7e4b2cdc620c872d025fe5a4e9.png)\n\nIdentify the points that lie on the line $y = x + 1$.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The plotted points are A=(2,7), B=(4,5), C=(7,2). Only B satisfies y=x+1."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055296 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ce9210e-8c33-56d3-a143-b8194c6e7d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439773} {:answer/id #uuid "15d84877-db47-53cc-adf7-15e463488793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce9210e-8c33-56d3-a143-b8194c6e7d2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439773} :answer-field/id #uuid "99529b71-fb0d-5b9b-adec-1b9531669fa6" :answer-field/key "Point $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440244} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1d3092-75b5-5c45-bb6e-b7fe0a349b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439775} {:answer/id #uuid "e8bd57e5-7e8e-551a-ba0e-d12a020c81be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/i