ext} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439856}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48a91d43-b10e-5fa5-ac58-14ddb60ffc8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439856} :answer-field/id #uuid "415c96ce-c78f-50f0-9f80-e3fc5b279dba" :answer-field/key "$y = 4 - x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440285}] :question/id #uuid "2fe51fc5-fce7-5fb6-911c-f561e72ff3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-59732" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d78eaaedd26a27d9163fdcddfce5c5ed429e441a75d361f0840935fce9235c6.png)\n\nWhich of the following gives the graph of the straight line above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The line has intercepts (0,4) and (4,0), so its equation is y=4-x, statement $y = 4 - x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059469 :question/id #uuid "762e323d-62be-5cd0-ad06-7b11af56fe3f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3136" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\sin^2\\theta$ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^2{\\theta}+\\cos^2{\\theta})\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\cos^2\\theta + \\sin^2\\theta = 1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{\\theta}+\\sin^2{\\theta}\\cos^2{\\theta} = \\sin^2\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059470 :question/id #uuid "f2b7e482-2bcd-5bd2-91ee-66415b375da4" :question/math-academy-id "e-3137" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta}\t=\t\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\cdot (\\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^2 \\theta)} {\\sin \\theta}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1)}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\cos \\theta \\sin^2 \\theta + \\cos^3 \\theta} {\\sin \\theta} = \\cot \\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059471 :question/id #uuid "9ee1e04e-8a36-5597-8928-c2ebd67c1b1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3139" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\cot{\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the second term using the identity $\\cot \\theta = \\dfrac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\dfrac{\\cos{\\theta}}{\\sin{\\theta}}\n$$\n\nNext, we put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )} &= \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\cdot (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )} &= \\frac{({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )} \\\\ &= \\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta (1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )} \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } \\\\ &= \\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\sin{\\theta}}{1+\\cos{\\theta}}+\\cot{\\theta} = \\csc\\theta.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059486 :question/id #uuid "d917e025-59a4-5df5-b412-4eb6f2c4afc7" :question/math-academy-id "e-3329" :question/problem "Simplify the expression $\\sin x(2\\cos x - \\sin x) - \\cos^2x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we expand the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we group the $\\sin^2 x$ and $\\cos^2 x$ terms. \n\n$$\n2\\sin x\\cos x -(\\sin^2x + \\cos^2 x)\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^2{x} + \\cos^2{x} = 1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n2\\sin x\\cos x - 1\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\sin x(2\\cos x - \\sin x) - \\cos^2x = 2\\sin x\\cos x - 1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059523 :question/id #uuid "1d2717f9-b905-59eb-85d7-6db4f9c9dc7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4292" :question/problem "Find $\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}$ if $\\mathbf{a}=-4\\mathbf{i}+6\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=12\\mathbf{i}$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}$, we just need to compute all of the $\\mathbf{i}$'s and $\\mathbf{j}$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 2b &= (-4i + 6j) - 2(12i) \\\\\n&=-4i + 6j - 24i \\\\\n&= (-4i - 24i) + 6j \\\\\n&=-28i + 6j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059524 :question/id #uuid "2cb63c87-320a-5cb4-b413-8c6bf9723641" :question/math-academy-id "e-4293" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -7, 15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 14, -11 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 3b &= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - 3 \\cdot ⟨14,-11⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - ⟨42,-33⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7 - 42, 15 - (-33)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 49, 48⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059525 :question/id #uuid "43cfef07-255d-5167-b815-267883918993" :question/math-academy-id "e-4294" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]},$ $\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}2 \\\\ 4\\end{array} \\right]},$ and $\\mathbf{c}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 3 \\\\ 7\\end{array} \\right]}.$ Find $2\\mathbf{a}-(\\mathbf{b}-5\\mathbf{c})$." :question/worked-solution "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a - (b - 5c) &= 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - 5 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ -31\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059526 :question/id #uuid "0adf8fad-9a6f-5eb1-970f-11633ba98ca1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4295" :question/problem "The vectors $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are given in the picture below. Find the coordinates of $\\vec{a}+6\\vec{b}$.\n\n![](images/56/56b10e759084da6fb21c8421bc9ff6d74aac2602df28f6c8e478bd874d7d6e9f.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the picture, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^(→) + 6b^(→) &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059545 :question/id #uuid "d2698dbf-dea6-5abb-970e-a3ace180e337" :question/math-academy-id "e-4341" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,-4,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle -7,0,2 \\rangle.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 2\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ -7 & 0\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 0)i-(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))j+(3\\cdot 0-(-4)\\cdot (-7))k \\\\  & =-8i-13j-28k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-13,-28⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059546 :question/id #uuid "b834e666-de4f-5964-a280-6571ad44b6bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4343" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3, 1, 2x \\rangle,$ $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 0,1,x \\rangle,$ and $|\\,\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\,| = \\sqrt{19}.$ Find $x.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2x \\\\ 0 & 1 & x\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2x \\\\ 1 & x\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2x \\\\ 0 & x\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =-xi-3xj+3k \\\\  & =⟨-x,-3x,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, computing the magnitude, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\times b\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-x)^{2}+(-3x)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLastly, we solve for $x$ the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & |\\,a\\times b\\,|=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & \\sqrt{10{x}^{2}+9}=\\sqrt{19} \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}+9=19 \\\\  & 10{x}^{2}=10 \\\\  & {x}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x= \\pm 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059557 :question/id #uuid "2b6e8845-a53d-510c-b44f-1b00271ee507" :question/math-academy-id "e-4434" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if <div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-10 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059558 :question/id #uuid "b066b73a-c777-550c-9c6e-af8093bf7fab" :question/math-academy-id "e-4435" :question/problem "Calculate $\\det(A),$ if <div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}-(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059559 :question/id #uuid "043a5e58-e1a0-50a5-b1be-d404e6262991" :question/math-academy-id "e-4436" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle {A} = \n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        2 & -1  \\\\\n        -3 & k\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n$$\nand\n$\\det({A}) = 5$, what is the value of $k?$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix} = ad - bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -3 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =2k-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=5,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =5 \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059980 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bef9d71-e6eb-54e4-8e8e-a529aa8f1992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241284} {:answer/id #uuid "af58227c-7285-5719-b8ee-6e95dc121818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242708} {:answer/id #uuid "b33e532a-b90d-5de2-812f-858d1ea4ce57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242741} {:answer/id #uuid "b7782812-7471-5927-8799-42fa4e8f2c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242786} {:answer/id #uuid "d690db23-f51d-5c54-a3fe-07d2f24b9b75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bef9d71-e6eb-54e4-8e8e-a529aa8f1992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241284} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd1e424-be57-57db-8709-ae267fc7b54a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67459f8a-4276-51e0-8ff0-10c56a6d248e" :question/math-academy-id "q-1079" :question/problem "Calculate $\\text{det}(A)$, if\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A) & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =0-6 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059981 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b466bee3-4694-50ff-b4ff-be40469939a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056245} {:answer/id #uuid "14252abb-f88d-5c80-a1a7-50e1c5101e76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056246} {:answer/id #uuid "422a8592-44c9-5cd7-a9f8-f218255dd350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2} - 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056247} {:answer/id #uuid "5403717f-fd25-5fdf-9147-cb1006233b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056248} {:answer/id #uuid "62819f9b-2032-516f-902f-f58dc1fc0aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6} - 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "422a8592-44c9-5cd7-a9f8-f218255dd350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2} - 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056247} :answer-field/id #uuid "49e48a24-3b9b-576a-ba9c-ed6114af8aa4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056244}] :question/id #uuid "50adc5c7-3aa8-5ed8-9f4a-a8650f063784" :question/math-academy-id "q-1088" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\n&=\\sqrt{2}\\cdot3-5\\cdot1 \\\\\n&=3\\sqrt{2}-5.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c21266-f6c2-5bea-9e7b-5c12a6cd64b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241696} {:answer/id #uuid "3e6a2a2e-5861-5f92-b070-b29670058f9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{x}-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241737} {:answer/id #uuid "404488cf-c12a-5d3e-8f12-bae9be5d6d67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241756} {:answer/id #uuid "95789385-1849-5307-a089-1a094f6dcc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}-2{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242493} {:answer/id #uuid "d8e15fa7-75e2-5444-be13-0b59e1863f69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-{y}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "404488cf-c12a-5d3e-8f12-bae9be5d6d67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-{y}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241756} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b79083a-ceaf-5ef9-8a92-8b480f0daf73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31d5493d-598a-5cd3-9717-dec41584eaba" :question/math-academy-id "q-1089" :question/problem "Calculate $det(Z)$, if\n $$\n\\displaystyle Z=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(Z) & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\sqrt{x} & y \\\\ {y}^{2} & \\sqrt{x}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{x}-y\\cdot {y}^{2} \\\\  & =x-{y}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060000 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adeef685-13ff-59be-8555-fa285a4b673e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056359} {:answer/id #uuid "e93e332c-0067-5a8e-978e-451498a19a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056360} {:answer/id #uuid "09a86a42-c0b8-57e0-a93a-e191a7d6b5f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056361} {:answer/id #uuid "0a801cc5-5312-593f-9422-e650a8b22f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056362} {:answer/id #uuid "3f33f5eb-9069-5dcd-955b-ccc0b698801b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "adeef685-13ff-59be-8555-fa285a4b673e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056359} :answer-field/id #uuid "809ecc7b-96f9-5877-beda-07f945eee167" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056358}] :question/id #uuid "ea87b1ac-4625-5a01-8d70-68a1975a00a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-11648" :question/problem "What is $\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}$?" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{vmatrix}\n&=2\\cdot7-(-4)\\cdot(-2) \\\\\n&=14-8 \\\\\n&=6.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0ff914a-1317-5490-ba59-b2437dd6665a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056365} {:answer/id #uuid "be028415-acff-5d6d-8080-1a4b0687fc37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056366} {:answer/id #uuid "28d6cf2e-8b16-58ce-af42-d46cb399a7f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056367} {:answer/id #uuid "3882486c-1efa-5685-9f10-e83963bf1488" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056368} {:answer/id #uuid "585ec4a5-edb5-5cf4-907c-653192911ffa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056369}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0ff914a-1317-5490-ba59-b2437dd6665a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056365} :answer-field/id #uuid "463bd4e4-2bee-5ee4-b6dd-f8a4f765f86b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056364}] :question/id #uuid "cda11aab-d0f1-5aed-9faf-9b4214024dc7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11651" :question/problem "If\n$$\n\\displaystyle C = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nand\n$det(C) = 3$, what is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{vmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{vmatrix}=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(C)&=\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & k\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&=2\\cdot k-3\\cdot5 \\\\\n&=2k-15.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(C)=3$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2k-15&=3 \\\\\n2k&=18 \\\\\nk&=9.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
